From: Jonas Karlsson <jonas.karlsson@qt.io>
Subject: [PATCH] PhysX: Ask for the mutex attributes the libc has

PhysX 5 has no Android platform of its own any more, so every Linux,
bionic and the OHOS musl included, takes the PX_LINUX paths of
FdUnixMutex.cpp, and those ask pthreads for more than either libc has:

- bionic defines no PTHREAD_PRIO_PROTECT and declares no
  pthread_mutexattr_setprioceiling(), so neither the protocol helpers nor
  the mutex constructor compiles for Android. It has no priority
  protected mutexes to configure at all, so leave the whole protocol out
  there, which puts Android back on the plain recursive mutex it got from
  PhysX 4.1, where it was a platform apart and none of this code was
  compiled for it. That also keeps the build off
  pthread_mutexattr_setprotocol(), which bionic only declares from API
  level 28 on.

- the OHOS SDK does define PTHREAD_PRIO_PROTECT and does declare
  pthread_mutexattr_setprotocol(), but not
  pthread_mutexattr_setprioceiling(), so only that one call needs to go.
  The ceiling it sets is 0, which is no priority ceiling any pthreads
  implementation accepts, and it only means anything for the protocol the
  OHOS mutexes cannot have anyway.

Plain musl and glibc keep every call they had.
---
 src/3rdparty/PhysX/source/foundation/unix/FdUnixMutex.cpp | 9 ++++++---
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/3rdparty/PhysX/source/foundation/unix/FdUnixMutex.cpp b/src/3rdparty/PhysX/source/foundation/unix/FdUnixMutex.cpp
--- a/src/3rdparty/PhysX/source/foundation/unix/FdUnixMutex.cpp
+++ b/src/3rdparty/PhysX/source/foundation/unix/FdUnixMutex.cpp
@@ -38,7 +38,7 @@
 namespace physx
 {
 
-#if PX_LINUX
+#if PX_LINUX && !defined(__BIONIC__)
 
 #include <sched.h>
 
@@ -69,7 +69,7 @@ int PxGetMutexProtocol()
 	return gMutexProtocol;
 }
 
-#endif //PX_LINUX
+#endif //PX_LINUX && !defined(__BIONIC__)
 
 
 namespace
@@ -91,8 +91,11 @@ PxMutexImpl::PxMutexImpl()
 	pthread_mutexattr_t attr;
 	pthread_mutexattr_init(&attr);
 	pthread_mutexattr_settype(&attr, PTHREAD_MUTEX_RECURSIVE);
-#if PX_LINUX
+#if PX_LINUX && !defined(__BIONIC__)
 	pthread_mutexattr_setprotocol(&attr, gMutexProtocol);
+#endif
+// the OHOS SDK declares no pthread_mutexattr_setprioceiling()
+#if PX_LINUX && !defined(__BIONIC__) && !defined(__OHOS__)
 	pthread_mutexattr_setprioceiling(&attr, 0);
 #endif
 	pthread_mutex_init(&getMutex(this)->lock, &attr);
